BorrowCapability
├── initialize
│   ├── when adapter, targets, token, minimum, query or offset are invalid
│   │   └── reverts factory creation atomically
│   └── given a scalar or tuple query for a fixed account
│       └── checks query shape and preserves the configured account
├── borrow
│   ├── when caller or selector differs from the configured one
│   │   └── reverts before protocol execution
│   ├── when the protocol call or token forwarding fails
│   │   └── rolls back debt, delegation and token transfers
│   ├── given protocol or forwarding callbacks
│   │   ├── rejects borrow reentry and minimum changes
│   │   └── reads health after the final token transfer
│   └── given the fixed post-borrow health query
│       ├── when the query fails or its selected word is absent
│       │   └── rolls back borrowing
│       ├── when health is below the nonzero floor
│       │   └── rolls back borrowing including direct-to-adapter transfers
│       └── when health equals or exceeds the floor
│           └── forwards only newly received tokens and returns protocol data
├── setMinHealthFactor
│   ├── rejects non-adapter callers and zero minimum
│   └── applies the new floor to subsequent borrowing
└── migrate
    ├── preserves protocol and health configuration
    └── rejects initialization data that would reconfigure them
